{"base_rate":0.6839378238341969,"brier":0.1973889464594128,"bss":0.08686775128332502,"bss_hi":0.17447711851705808,"bss_lo":-0.019751133523470497,"chart":{"base":[948.8,73.3],"fp":[376.0,328.7],"note":{"base":"skill 0.09 — higher than 15% of cities","fp":"low end +17pp, high end +9pp","rel":"promised 20% → rained 38%; promised 100% → rained 88%"},"rel":"189.2,300.7 414,198 552.5,158.5 637.6,124.3 689,85.2"},"country":"LC","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve"],"ece":0.11423143350604492,"ess":356.2867292735953,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Castries</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Castries rain forecast is only marginally better than quoting the long-run average, though 5 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (100%), believe about\n<b>88%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(11%), there is still roughly a <b>28%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 579 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-03-25. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nthe station, 2.4 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.09, ranked 180 of\n213 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(156&ndash;190) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>11%</td><td class='num'><b>28%</b></td><td class='num'>58</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>30%</td><td class='num'><b>49%</b></td><td class='num'>57</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>49%</td><td class='num'><b>62%</b></td><td class='num'>58</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>64%</td><td class='num'><b>62%</b></td><td class='num'>50</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>75%</td><td class='num'><b>71%</b></td><td class='num'>65</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>82%</td><td class='num'><b>72%</b></td><td class='num'>46</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>89%</td><td class='num'><b>72%</b></td><td class='num'>71</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>95%</td><td class='num'><b>92%</b></td><td class='num'>39</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>100%</td><td class='num'><b>88%</b></td><td class='num'>135</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">5 of 9 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Castries</b> <span class=\"muted\">Saint Lucia</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag bad\">Barely beats the average</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">5 points off by more than chance</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>0.09</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>156&ndash;190\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 213</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>579 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Castries &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Castries\"><rect clas